  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Continous Multipurpose Household Survey - Continous Multipurpose Household Survey VSAT</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Hush&#xe5;llsunders&#xf6;kn  Faso  enk&#xe4;t statistikst&#xf6;d</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In April 2012, a request was received from the Government of Burkina Faso to finance a household survey (Enqu&#xea;te Multisectorielle Continue/Multisectoral continue survey). The main objectives of this survey are to establish a permanent system to collect data to feed main indicators for the national development strategy and MDGs. In the proposed Plan for phasing out Sweden&#x2019;s development cooperation with Burkina Faso 2013-2016, pro-poor sustainable growth is one of the three sectors for Swedish support. The total of amount is SEK 15 million for two years, 2013 and 2014.&#xa0;
Six amendments were signed on 20 May 2015, 31 August 2015, 22 December 2015, 04 August 2016, 18 January 2017 and 20 October 2017, respectively. These amendments were made to allow both the continuation of the activities which has been delayed and, secondly, the consolidation of the achievements by the preparation of the second phase of this relevant household survey.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen syftar till att st&#xf6;dja inr&#xe4;ttandet av ett flexibelt och      kostnadseffektivt system f&#xf6;r regelbundna hush&#xe5;llsunders&#xf6;kningar som   den nationella statistikmyndigheten i Burkina Faso (INSD) genomf&#xf6;r.   Systemet ska till&#xe5;ta insamling av relevant och uppdaterad             socio-ekonomisk information f&#xf6;r att kunna f&#xf6;lja upp genomf&#xf6;rande och  utfall av den nationella utvecklingsstrategin och milleniem&#xe5;len.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to support the establishment of a flexible and       cost-effective system of regular household surveys in the national    statistical authority in Burkina Faso (INSD). The system should allow the collection of relevant and updated socio-economic information in  order to monitor the implementation and outcomes of the national      development strategy and the MDGs.</narrative>
  </description>
